Glances on FenrirOS
===================

`glances` runs the curses interface straight away. Optional extras:

    cp /usr/share/doc/glances/glances.conf.example /etc/glances/glances.conf

(Glances reads /etc/glances/glances.conf, ~/.config/glances/glances.conf.)

The web interface and REST API are the dinit service glances-web, installed
inert (not enabled):

    dinitctl enable glances-web

It listens on 127.0.0.1:61208 as the `glances` user, with no password. To
serve it to the network edit /etc/dinit.d/glances-web (`--bind`) and add
a password with `glances -w --password` (creates a hashed password file in
~/.config/glances) or put a reverse proxy with authentication in front of
it. Run as root instead of glances for the sensors and processes that
otherwise are hidden.

Not available in this package: the optional PyJWT token authentication for
the REST API and exporters other than Prometheus/ZeroMQ/CSV/JSON.
